language-derived-from-the-record-11 = unlines (cons "**9. From physics up, with no break.** A participant's record is everything it has received, and the meaning of a present occurrence is the family of what followed the past occurrences its context selects, transported to now. Any coupling of two physical systems is a channel: one system's change of state enters the other's record. For the receiver a signal means the transported family of what followed its past occurrences: an animal's alarm call, the predator, the flight. Language is the same construction with larger occurrence types and with copying across individuals, which joins their records into the human superorganism's one record; before humans the copying ran through DNA, the singular autocatalytic reaction's own record. Nothing new enters between physical interaction and words." nil)
